WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.037 --> 00:00:01.530
- "Halloween 5" is a movie

00:00:01.530 --> 00:00:03.600
that raises more questions than answers,

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:05.830
but it answers at least one
thing I was wondering about,

00:00:05.830 --> 00:00:08.450
but probably nobody else
cared about in "Halloween 4".

00:00:08.450 --> 00:00:11.010
Number five would be "The
Revenge of Michael Myers",

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.790
and the opening is a
continuation of the ending of 4,

00:00:13.790 --> 00:00:16.320
where Michael was shot
repeatedly and falls into a hole.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:17.840
Here we see what happened next,

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.560
which may be a little
nod to how "Halloween II"

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.050
handled its intro and
wouldn't be the only one.

00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:23.360
Michael escapes through this tunnel

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.270
to make it to a river

00:00:24.270 --> 00:00:26.020
where he floats downstream to escape.

00:00:26.020 --> 00:00:28.720
I'm reminded of this line
from Reverend Jackson Sayer,

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:31.440
who gives Dr. Loomis a lift
early on in "Halloween 4".

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:33.540
Many of his lines fit in
with the theme of fate

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:35.550
seen in that movie, which
you can hear all about

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.760
in the previous episode
of Things You Missed.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.999
But there are a couple that
just seem like weird lines,

00:00:39.999 --> 00:00:41.440
like this one.

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.260
- I saw it on your face
back there in the dust.

00:00:44.260 --> 00:00:47.110
I saw it clear as breasts
in blue suede shoes.

00:00:47.110 --> 00:00:49.690
- Which I still don't really understand,

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:51.500
but there's also this hymn that he sings

00:00:51.500 --> 00:00:52.985
at the end of his scene.

00:00:52.985 --> 00:00:57.480
- ♪ Yes, we'll gather at the river ♪

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:02.080
♪ The beautiful, beautiful river ♪

00:01:02.080 --> 00:01:03.800
- Could this have been a foreshadowing

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.200
that Michael's supposed fate

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.170
was going to be in this river?

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.950
Whatever the plans were for "Halloween 4",

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:11.310
it's pretty clear that the
next sequel changed them.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.820
To learn how "Halloween 5"

00:01:12.820 --> 00:01:15.970
attempted to honor its
predecessors (somewhat poorly),

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:18.371
stick around to the end of this video.

00:01:18.371 --> 00:01:20.788
(dark music)

00:01:24.357 --> 00:01:26.500
"Halloween 5" would, as always,

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:28.660
not bring back the
previous movie's director,

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:29.860
in this case, Dwight Little,

00:01:29.860 --> 00:01:32.040
who seemingly just wanted
to quit while he was ahead.

00:01:32.040 --> 00:01:33.600
To pronounce the new director's name,

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:36.000
I give you Halloween expert and Frenchman,

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.420
Jimmy Champane.

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:40.100
- Dominique Othenin-Girard
is the correct pronunciation,

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.040
and despite the fact that
my last name is Champane,

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.570
I'm not actually from France.

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:46.210
I did a video on "Halloween
5" a few years ago,

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.600
and I had to learn exactly
how to say that name.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:50.480
When I saw "Halloween
4" for the first time

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:52.830
and specifically how it
ended, it really affected me

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:54.980
because I was the same age as Jamie,

00:01:54.980 --> 00:01:56.540
and I really wanted her to win.

00:01:56.540 --> 00:01:58.640
But over the years and
after seeing "Halloween 5"

00:01:58.640 --> 00:01:59.970
and where the story went from there,

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.880
I think it actually could
have been kind of cool

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:03.870
to see Jamie take up the knife and mask.

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:04.770
If you think about it though,

00:02:04.770 --> 00:02:06.370
it's absolutely insane that this ending

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:07.780
was green-lit in the first place,

00:02:07.780 --> 00:02:10.440
because the only reason
"Halloween 4" exists

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:12.090
is because people were so mad

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:14.390
that Michael Myers was
killed off in "Halloween II"

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:16.190
and then not featured in "Halloween III".

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:17.350
The point I'm trying to make is that

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:18.920
as the Halloween franchise went on,

00:02:18.920 --> 00:02:20.740
there was a clear divide
between the producers,

00:02:20.740 --> 00:02:22.070
the filmmakers and the fans,

00:02:22.070 --> 00:02:25.150
and this movie suffers the
most out of any of them for it.

00:02:25.150 --> 00:02:27.430
- To try to change things up a little bit,

00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:30.730
(I guess) Girard tries to
humanize Michael Myers,

00:02:30.730 --> 00:02:33.973
which kind of defeats the
point of Michael Myers.

00:02:35.700 --> 00:02:37.530
- Calling the mask in "Halloween 5" a mess

00:02:37.530 --> 00:02:38.990
would be the understatement of the year,

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:40.260
but it's actually pretty interesting

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.080
that it was sculpted by Greg Nicotero

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:43.930
of "The Walking Dead"
and "Creepshow" fame.

00:02:43.930 --> 00:02:45.410
I've always struggled to understand why

00:02:45.410 --> 00:02:48.440
instead of using the mask from
"Halloween 4" in this movie,

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.750
because that movie's ending

00:02:49.750 --> 00:02:51.630
bleeds directly into this movie's,

00:02:51.630 --> 00:02:54.740
they just sculpted a new one
after Greg Nicotero's head,

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.390
which is why it has a teardrop shape

00:02:56.390 --> 00:02:58.600
and looked completely
different than any other mask

00:02:58.600 --> 00:02:59.610
in the franchise.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:01.430
- I don't really know
what his motivation was

00:03:01.430 --> 00:03:04.330
for making a character so
well-known and well-stated

00:03:04.330 --> 00:03:06.580
to be inhuman seemed more humanized.

00:03:06.580 --> 00:03:09.040
It sounds like he just has
this weird crush on The Shape.

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.640
- Such a vulnerable little girl

00:03:11.640 --> 00:03:16.640
against a massive, amazing
strong man who nothing stops

00:03:17.490 --> 00:03:19.270
when he has an idea in his mind.

00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:20.480
He just goes straight.

00:03:20.480 --> 00:03:22.770
- But something tells me you don't.

00:03:22.770 --> 00:03:25.130
That being said, we've talked
about the first four movies,

00:03:25.130 --> 00:03:26.610
so we might as well do these ones.

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:29.064
Let's get into the things you missed.

00:03:29.064 --> 00:03:32.897
(eerie music, knives slicing)

00:03:33.930 --> 00:03:36.070
I'll actually admit that
the opening title sequence

00:03:36.070 --> 00:03:38.090
to "Halloween 5" is a little bit creative.

00:03:38.090 --> 00:03:39.500
In one and two, we see a pumpkin

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:41.200
over a black screen with the credits.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.620
In three, we see the credits play

00:03:42.620 --> 00:03:44.340
over this digital display of a pumpkin

00:03:44.340 --> 00:03:46.610
to fit the sci-fi/horror
genre of that movie.

00:03:46.610 --> 00:03:48.750
And in four, we just see
more of a pumpkin patch

00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:50.060
and some other stuff.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:52.010
So five kind of reinvents that concept

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.830
by cutting in quick slices of a pumpkin

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.190
being massacred by a knife,

00:03:55.190 --> 00:03:57.310
some of which are shot
from inside the pumpkin.

00:03:57.310 --> 00:03:58.160
This would be the movie

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.240
where we really go inside Michael Myers

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.880
for better or for worse.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.100
- I'm gonna go with better.

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.280
No, worse, it's definitely worse.

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:07.480
- As I mentioned, Michael
escapes his hunters

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.370
by letting the river carry him downstream,

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:11.948
where he meets a hobo
and his pet bird, Tippi.

00:04:11.948 --> 00:04:14.290
- There's nothing out there, Tippi.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:15.760
- In our "Halloween" 1 video,

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.610
we talked about how characters
like Loomis, Marion and Leigh

00:04:18.610 --> 00:04:20.050
were all named after characters

00:04:20.050 --> 00:04:22.860
from Alfred Hitchcock's
classic horror film, "Psycho".

00:04:22.860 --> 00:04:24.770
For this reason, I
think Tippi may be named

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:25.910
after the actress that debuted

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.160
in Alfred Hitchcock's
"The Birds", Tippi Hedrin.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:29.350
- Anyway, a year has gone by

00:04:29.350 --> 00:04:31.410
and Jamie is still
regularly having nightmares

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:33.430
about her uncle, and she's also gone mute

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:35.960
as part of the trauma she
experienced last Halloween.

00:04:35.960 --> 00:04:37.490
This is a very heavy-handed sign

00:04:37.490 --> 00:04:38.770
that she's connected to Michael,

00:04:38.770 --> 00:04:40.450
and that her visions are actually her

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:42.270
seeing through The Shape's eyes.

00:04:42.270 --> 00:04:44.130
But looking back, this
is also definitely part

00:04:44.130 --> 00:04:46.360
of the director's attempt
to humanize Michael Myers,

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:48.830
which was like his main
goal going into this movie.

00:04:48.830 --> 00:04:49.930
I don't know if you guys knew that.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:52.170
I mean, if I was making the
middle movie in a trilogy

00:04:52.170 --> 00:04:53.650
five movies into a franchise,

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:55.280
that's about when I would switch things up

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:57.710
and completely change the
motivations of the main villain.

00:04:57.710 --> 00:04:59.610
In the last movie, Jamie
is one of the survivors.

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:00.810
She's who we empathize with.

00:05:00.810 --> 00:05:02.870
She's who we're rooting for
through the entire thing.

00:05:02.870 --> 00:05:05.160
Michael Myers doesn't
talk, now she doesn't talk.

00:05:05.160 --> 00:05:06.760
It's how we relate to
him a little bit better.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:08.480
I don't really think it
makes a lot of sense.

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:10.380
- Last year, Jamie wore a clown costume

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:11.910
just as Michael had many years ago,

00:05:11.910 --> 00:05:13.800
but this year she goes as a princess.

00:05:13.800 --> 00:05:15.560
You may remember the
princess in clown drawings

00:05:15.560 --> 00:05:16.920
on her door in "Halloween 4",

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:18.360
so this choice represents the idea

00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:19.980
that she's now going down the good path

00:05:19.980 --> 00:05:21.180
rather than the evil one.

00:05:21.180 --> 00:05:24.000
However, she can't fully get
rid of the clown and the evil.

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.920
She still has dreams about that night.

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:27.340
The care facility that she's staying in

00:05:27.340 --> 00:05:29.750
is decorated with items
like a balloon-themed lamp,

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:32.130
this clown light switch, a
clown-themed height chart,

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.240
and this absolutely comforting clown

00:05:34.240 --> 00:05:36.623
placed in her room to watch her sleep.

00:05:37.660 --> 00:05:39.480
We also see a clown doll at her home,

00:05:39.480 --> 00:05:41.360
even though she never
goes there in this movie.

00:05:41.360 --> 00:05:43.510
You would think maybe the
people taking care of her

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:45.150
would put all of this clown stuff away

00:05:45.150 --> 00:05:47.320
to avoid bringing back those bad memories,

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:49.100
but it seems they've just opted for the

00:05:49.100 --> 00:05:51.330
get-over-it-sooner-rather-than-later
approach.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.940
The other survivor is
Rachel, her adoptive sister.

00:05:53.940 --> 00:05:56.302
She gets home to get ready
for a Halloween party.

00:05:56.302 --> 00:05:57.367
(phone rings)

00:05:57.367 --> 00:05:58.680
- Ugh, I'm coming.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:05:59.970
- Why does she yell "I'm coming"

00:05:59.970 --> 00:06:01.300
as she's running to the phone?

00:06:01.300 --> 00:06:03.000
Like, she does realize
the caller can't hear her

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:05.220
until after she picks
up the receiver, right?

00:06:05.220 --> 00:06:06.790
- Can someone give me one good reason

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:08.860
why they decided to do Rachel so dirty?

00:06:08.860 --> 00:06:10.890
She was one of the best characters.

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:12.540
- Loomis warns her to
get out of the house,

00:06:12.540 --> 00:06:13.870
and then she's just out of breath

00:06:13.870 --> 00:06:15.870
upon reaching the edge
of her own property.

00:06:15.870 --> 00:06:17.740
Time to hit the cardio, Rachel.

00:06:17.740 --> 00:06:19.210
At this point, the cops show up

00:06:19.210 --> 00:06:22.274
accompanied by circus
music for some reason.

00:06:22.274 --> 00:06:24.720
(silly squeaking music)

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:26.410
And no, we didn't add that.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:28.542
That's just the music that's in the movie.

00:06:28.542 --> 00:06:31.760
(silly squeaking music)

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.750
- It honestly took me years of rewatches

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:36.110
to notice this music that
plays underneath the cops.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:39.120
There is so much bizarre shit
going on in "Halloween 5"

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.040
that it didn't even
register as weird to me.

00:06:41.040 --> 00:06:42.690
- At this point, we start to see Michael

00:06:42.690 --> 00:06:45.140
acting differently than
he has in other movies,

00:06:45.140 --> 00:06:48.173
but he would not be the only one.

00:06:48.173 --> 00:06:52.006
(dark music, thunder rumbles)

00:06:52.990 --> 00:06:55.490
(eerie music)

00:06:56.880 --> 00:06:57.970
- In the original "Halloween" movies,

00:06:57.970 --> 00:07:00.550
Michael Myers is shown to
be this unstoppable force.

00:07:00.550 --> 00:07:02.880
He stalks and comes
after his victim slowly

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:04.140
and he shows no mercy.

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:05.610
In this one, there are multiple points

00:07:05.610 --> 00:07:06.820
where he doesn't kill a victim

00:07:06.820 --> 00:07:08.430
even though he has a clear chance to,

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:10.340
and I've thought about
this a lot over the years,

00:07:10.340 --> 00:07:12.270
and the only explanation
I can come up with

00:07:12.270 --> 00:07:14.360
is that this is yet
another shallow attempt

00:07:14.360 --> 00:07:15.920
to humanize Michael Myers.

00:07:15.920 --> 00:07:17.740
For example, he sees Rachel in the house,

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:19.840
he puts his hand on
the clothing rack here,

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:21.470
and instead of doing anything about it,

00:07:21.470 --> 00:07:23.510
he just walks out of the room right after.

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:24.380
What happened there?

00:07:24.380 --> 00:07:26.180
Did he leave his Viagra in the car?

00:07:26.180 --> 00:07:28.650
Something similar happens
as he watches Sammy and Tina

00:07:28.650 --> 00:07:30.350
outside the hospital later that day,

00:07:30.350 --> 00:07:31.510
but doesn't make his move.

00:07:31.510 --> 00:07:33.310
Then later on, once the killing has begun,

00:07:33.310 --> 00:07:35.950
he finds himself behind the
wheel of a large automobile.

00:07:35.950 --> 00:07:37.650
We all know that Michael Myers walks slow

00:07:37.650 --> 00:07:38.980
because that's part of his character.

00:07:38.980 --> 00:07:40.510
It's been established from the beginning.

00:07:40.510 --> 00:07:43.620
But is there any reason he
has to drive slow as well?

00:07:43.620 --> 00:07:46.170
The only logical explanation
is that he's taking time

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:48.000
to enjoy stalking his victims.

00:07:48.000 --> 00:07:50.300
The corpse shrine he builds in
the attic of the Myers house,

00:07:50.300 --> 00:07:52.170
which by the way, is completely different

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:53.920
than the one we've seen
in the other movies

00:07:53.920 --> 00:07:55.420
suggest that there's an art to the way

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:56.990
that Michael Myers does his killing.

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:58.940
That, along with when he stops his rampage

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:00.170
to listen to Loomis tell him

00:08:00.170 --> 00:08:02.060
how he might be able to cure his rage,

00:08:02.060 --> 00:08:03.960
and then again, when Jamie calls him uncle

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:05.940
are clear signs that maybe he does have

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:07.439
a human side after all.

00:08:07.439 --> 00:08:09.240
And that's when they take it too far

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:11.810
by making this bad-ass
slasher start crying.

00:08:11.810 --> 00:08:13.740
- Michael is not the only one to undergo

00:08:13.740 --> 00:08:15.450
a change in behavior in this movie.

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:16.720
If he's becoming more human,

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:19.430
I think maybe Dr. Loomis
is becoming less human.

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:21.380
Billy is a fellow patient
at Jamie's clinic,

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:23.400
and I think they bond
over their speech issues.

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:25.940
He has a stutter and she's
unable to speak at all anymore.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:27.750
When little Billy comes
in to check on Jamie

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:28.730
and see if she's okay,

00:08:28.730 --> 00:08:32.150
Loomis just ushers him out
and slams the door on him.

00:08:32.150 --> 00:08:32.983
- Slam!

00:08:32.983 --> 00:08:34.250
- The way that he talks to Jamie

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:37.043
is perhaps the scariest
part of this movie.

00:08:37.043 --> 00:08:39.363
(crashing)

00:08:39.363 --> 00:08:41.730
- What about your stepmother, Jamie?

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:43.160
(Zac laughs)
- What?

00:08:43.160 --> 00:08:45.140
- Then he also tells Jamie that Michael

00:08:45.140 --> 00:08:47.168
dug up the corpse of a nine-year-old girl,

00:08:47.168 --> 00:08:49.710
which we never see happen,

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:52.996
so did he just make that up to scare her?

00:08:52.996 --> 00:08:54.850
(creepy laughing)

00:08:54.850 --> 00:08:55.760
And then the finale,

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.540
without telling her the plan or anything,

00:08:57.540 --> 00:08:59.770
he just offers her up to Michael.

00:08:59.770 --> 00:09:00.603
- You want her?

00:09:02.124 --> 00:09:03.430
Here she is.

00:09:03.430 --> 00:09:05.140
- [Zac] No disrespect to Donald Pleasence,

00:09:05.140 --> 00:09:07.330
but Loomis should just
be shot at this point.

00:09:07.330 --> 00:09:09.810
Now I only noticed one
crew reference easter egg,

00:09:09.810 --> 00:09:12.290
and that is the badge of
this police officer Markland,

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:14.380
which references the prop
master in "Halloween 5",

00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:15.600
Sean E. Markland.

00:09:15.600 --> 00:09:17.610
However, there were also some callbacks

00:09:17.610 --> 00:09:18.960
to other "Halloween" movies.

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:21.120
So let's just start with "Halloween" 1.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:22.760
- I like that movie,
so I'll take this one.

00:09:22.760 --> 00:09:24.990
There are a ton of
references to mundane details

00:09:24.990 --> 00:09:25.870
in the original movie,

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.370
like this conversation
between Sammy and Tina.

00:09:28.370 --> 00:09:30.773
- [Tina] Sammy, why don't
you bag Spitz tonight?

00:09:31.746 --> 00:09:32.680
- [Sammy] I couldn't do that.

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:33.515
- Oh, sure you could.

00:09:33.515 --> 00:09:35.250
- Oh, no I can't.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:37.140
- [Jimmy] Which is essentially
the same conversation

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:38.920
that Annie and Laurie have in the car.

00:09:38.920 --> 00:09:40.640
- Sure you could, all you have to do

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.752
is go up to somebody and say,

00:09:42.752 --> 00:09:44.810
"You want to go to the dance?"

00:09:44.810 --> 00:09:46.300
- You could do that, I couldn't.

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:47.890
- The way that Michael slams on the brakes

00:09:47.890 --> 00:09:50.020
when Tina asks him to
stop at the gas station

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:52.280
is eerily reminiscent
of exactly what he does

00:09:52.280 --> 00:09:53.280
in "Halloween" 1.

00:09:53.280 --> 00:09:55.760
The way that Jamie sees Michael
standing outside her window

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:58.600
is also exactly how Laurie
sees him outside her window

00:09:58.600 --> 00:09:59.650
in "Halloween" 1.

00:09:59.650 --> 00:10:00.870
And then of course, there's a scene

00:10:00.870 --> 00:10:02.590
where Jamie is chased
through clothes lines

00:10:02.590 --> 00:10:04.370
which have large sheets hanging on them.

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:05.360
That's something we talked about

00:10:05.360 --> 00:10:07.190
in the videos for "Halloween" 1 and 2,

00:10:07.190 --> 00:10:08.930
and it's actually great
to see that this movie

00:10:08.930 --> 00:10:11.640
is going back to basics by
making most of the victims

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:13.460
teenagers who want to get laid.

00:10:13.460 --> 00:10:15.450
- [Tina] You guys wanna
come skinny dipping?

00:10:15.450 --> 00:10:16.680
- Are you serious, Tina?

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:18.690
This is the same chick who
just got done complaining

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:20.400
that it was too cold
standing outside the car

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:21.233
for two seconds.

00:10:21.233 --> 00:10:23.920
Now she wants to go skinny
dipping in Illinois in October?

00:10:23.920 --> 00:10:25.480
There are also a couple of similarities

00:10:25.480 --> 00:10:28.000
to "Halloween II" and
"Halloween 4" in this one,

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:29.760
like the false scare involving someone

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:31.050
dressed up as Michael Myers.

00:10:31.050 --> 00:10:33.500
We've also seen several
examples of the opposite,

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:34.650
where Michael is disguised

00:10:34.650 --> 00:10:36.370
as one of the regular human characters.

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:37.400
This time, it's another guy

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:39.380
who happens to be named Michael.

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:41.170
- Michael, open the door.

00:10:41.170 --> 00:10:43.660
- The movie also brings back
the "Halloween 4" concept

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.180
of Jamie riding on someone's
back to escape out a window,

00:10:46.180 --> 00:10:48.780
and continues the tradition
from "Halloween" 1 and 4

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:50.810
of taking out a dog very early on.

00:10:50.810 --> 00:10:53.100
When we see the shrine of all
of his victims in the attic

00:10:53.100 --> 00:10:55.840
and Jamie sees the dog,
it still barks somehow.

00:10:55.840 --> 00:10:57.550
Also half the jump scares in this movie

00:10:57.550 --> 00:10:58.683
are from animals.

00:10:59.601 --> 00:11:01.768
(screams)

00:11:04.050 --> 00:11:06.290
I do not know how there's
just like a picture

00:11:06.290 --> 00:11:07.690
of Coraline's mom right here,

00:11:07.690 --> 00:11:10.690
or how Dr. Disrespect manages
to show up on a wanted poster.

00:11:10.690 --> 00:11:12.580
I do not know why there's
this weird jump cut

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:14.380
when Mikey is getting jumped by Michael.

00:11:14.380 --> 00:11:16.980
I do not know why this lady
looks directly at the camera,

00:11:16.980 --> 00:11:19.210
and I do not know why the
end credits feel the need

00:11:19.210 --> 00:11:22.190
to specify that the names
represent the cast of characters

00:11:22.190 --> 00:11:24.290
as if we've never seen a movie before.

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:25.190
- And also real quick,

00:11:25.190 --> 00:11:27.410
did they think we wouldn't
notice that this is dubbed?

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:29.259
- We just had a distress
call from the clinic.

00:11:29.259 --> 00:11:31.170
They haven't been able
to reach them again.

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:32.400
There were four men up there.

00:11:32.400 --> 00:11:35.450
- There is one character that
we have not mentioned yet,

00:11:35.450 --> 00:11:37.950
and that is... Moleman.

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:39.910
No, I'm talking about Dr. Terence Wynn

00:11:39.910 --> 00:11:42.270
who is basically just an
unsolved mystery in this movie,

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:43.817
but would return in the next movie,

00:11:43.817 --> 00:11:45.570
"The Curse of Michael Myers".

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:48.430
As the name implies, Michael
Myers will also be returning

00:11:48.430 --> 00:11:49.370
in the sixth movie,

00:11:49.370 --> 00:11:51.197
which would be the last
of what is now called

00:11:51.197 --> 00:11:52.470
"The Thorn Trilogy".

00:11:52.470 --> 00:11:54.210
What I will about the cult of Thorn

00:11:54.210 --> 00:11:56.100
is it would have been
cool if its introduction

00:11:56.100 --> 00:11:58.730
opened up the series to more
powerful and evil entities

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.050
outside of just The Shape.

00:12:00.050 --> 00:12:02.600
So naturally, as with
the ideas of Halloween

00:12:02.600 --> 00:12:05.930
being an anthology franchise
and Jamie being an antagonist,

00:12:05.930 --> 00:12:07.530
that is not what happened.

00:12:07.530 --> 00:12:08.930
But before we venture forward

00:12:08.930 --> 00:12:11.130
to the end of "Halloween's"
original timeline,

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:13.450
make sure you grab your
baret, bake your baguette

00:12:13.450 --> 00:12:16.380
and head on over to the
wonderful channel of Champane.

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:17.410
- [Jimmy] If you haven't
checked it out yet,

00:12:17.410 --> 00:12:18.750
there's rankings, short films

00:12:18.750 --> 00:12:20.530
and tons of other videos to dig through.

00:12:20.530 --> 00:12:22.360
So remember to subscribe to CZsWorld

00:12:22.360 --> 00:12:23.750
for new horrors every week,

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:25.860
ring the death bell for all notifications,

00:12:25.860 --> 00:12:29.210
and we'll see you in the next
one, assuming we both survive.

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:31.950
- Did you just steal my line?

00:12:31.950 --> 00:12:32.870
Okay, change of plans.

00:12:32.870 --> 00:12:35.220
Jimmy will not be joining
us in the next vide--

